title: 'sc-executor: timed runtime calls with execution timeouts via wasmtime epoch interruption'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `create_timed_runtime` / `WasmtimeTimedRuntime` / `WasmtimeTimedInstance` (behind new
    `TimedWasmModule` / `TimedWasmInstance` traits) — wasm runtimes compiled with wasmtime
    epoch interruption whose calls take a mandatory execution timeout, failing with the new
    `Error::ExecutionTimeout`.

    New `WasmExecutor::call_with_execution_timeout` makes a timed runtime call through the
    normal executor machinery. For wasmtime, the timed counterpart of a cached runtime is
    compiled in a background thread; timed calls block until it is ready and always run on a
    fresh, non-pooled instance. PolkaVM has no execution-interruption mechanism: timed calls
    share the untimed module and run uncapped, with a one-time startup warning.
crates:
- name: sc-executor
  bump: minor
- name: sc-executor-common
  bump: major
- name: sc-executor-wasmtime
  bump: minor
- name: sc-executor-polkavm
  bump: major
